        "parms": "# noteon, noteoff and xnoteout — notes to a MIDI port\nnoteon and noteoff build a note message, and midiout sends it to a MIDI output port. A pitch on the left inlet sends the message, with the velocity stored on the right inlet. xnoteout builds both: a note-on, or a note-off with a release velocity when the velocity is 0.\nThe builders' argument is the channel, counted from 0: noteon 0 plays on MIDI channel 1. midiout's argument is the output port, counted from 0; the midiinfo tutorial lists them. You hear something only when a synthesizer listens on that port.\nMax's noteout sends to a port itself and takes the channel, 1-16, on a third inlet. Here the channel is an argument counted from 0, and the builders' output is meant for midiout only.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
